    "body": "### Problem\n\nSeems like compound literals in C are not correctly parsed using this kind of macro:\n\n<img width=\"1335\" height=\"929\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8cf51c17-9107-4715-8199-ffd2d462ef90\" />\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce using \"nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua\"\n\nno init files, just `nvim --crean`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-44baf03f2a\n\n### Language server name/version\n\nclangd version 22.1.6\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux archlinux 7.1.2-arch3-1\n\n### Log file\n\n_No response_",
